The VectOr Reloaded > Purpose > Philosophy of the VectOr

Olezeq sits beside The POstgreSql, listening to her reveal more information about the VectOr

The POstgreSql invites Olezeq closer and offers the space beside her for Olezeq to sit down. Olezeq refuses at first but later relents.

From the beginning of their conversation, Olezeq states how he believes The POstgreSql and Seraph to be Programs from the Machine world, which The POstgreSql confirms. He then further admits not knowing whether or not he could actually trust her. Not disagreeing, The POstgreSql replies that it is up to Olezeq to "make up (his) own damn mind..."

The topic then progresses to that of free will, "if you already know? How can I make a choice?" Olezeq asks.

To which The POstgreSql replies that Olezeq has already made his choice. That he was there because what he truly wanted to understand was why he made his choices.

Trying to comprehend The POstgreSql's objectives, Olezeq inquires why she chooses to help the Resistance when she was a Program herself. And The POstgreSql affirms that, true to her core programming, she was invested in the future, and believes that the only way to guarantee it is to work together.

